# Wrapper scopes for `Definitions`

> Module DefinitionsWrappers

> Using Definitions as Src

Generated by `cutecat_scripts/generate_dataset.py`; edits are
overwritten. Each scope below adds no rule: it declares one input
per parameter of a top-level function of the port and returns what
that function returns. CUTECat explores one entry point per run,
and a top-level function is not one until something names it.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope FnCountryOf:
  input c content Src.City
  output result content Src.Country

declaration scope FnSizeSum:
  input it content Src.Item
  output result content integer

declaration scope FnOriginCountry:
  input t content Src.Itinerary
  output result content Src.Country

declaration scope FnDestinationCountry:
  input t content Src.Itinerary
  output result content Src.Country

declaration scope FnTouches:
  input t content Src.Itinerary
  input cs content list of Src.Country
  output result content boolean

declaration scope FnWithin:
  input t content Src.Itinerary
  input cs content list of Src.Country
  output result content boolean

```

```catala
scope FnCountryOf:
  definition result equals Src.country_of of c

scope FnSizeSum:
  definition result equals Src.size_sum of it

scope FnOriginCountry:
  definition result equals Src.origin_country of t

scope FnDestinationCountry:
  definition result equals Src.destination_country of t

scope FnTouches:
  definition result equals Src.touches of t, cs

scope FnWithin:
  definition result equals Src.within of t, cs

```
